NAME
       intro - introduction to PureC OS commands

SYNOPSIS
       man intro

DESCRIPTION
       PureC OS is a 64-bit operating system written in C. Commands are small
       programs in /bin, /usr/bin and /sbin that read text, write text and can
       be combined with pipes in sh(1). Every command has a manual page; man -k
       WORD searches them.

COMMANDS
       Files     ls cat cp mv rm mkdir rmdir touch chmod stat find tree du df install realpath basename dirname
       Text      grep head tail wc sort uniq cut tr tee cmp diff nl rev seq xxd less echo
       System    ps kill free uptime date uname whoami id hostname env which sleep clear
       Power     reboot poweroff shutdown halt
       Network   ping curl
       Help      man help apropos whatis

EXAMPLES
       ls -l | grep .c | sort
       find / -name "*.txt" | xargs wc -l
       man -k .

SEE ALSO
       help(1), man(1), sh(1)
